ime's up!\" when the timer reaches zero.</p>\n    <pre><code>const timerDisplay = document.getElementById('timerDisplay');\nlet timeLeft = 300; // 5 minutes in seconds\n\nfunction updateTimer() {\n    let minutes = Math.floor(timeLeft / 60);\n    let seconds = timeLeft % 60;\n    seconds = seconds &lt; 10 ? '0' + seconds : seconds;\n    timerDisplay.textContent = `${minutes}:${seconds}`;\n    timeLeft--;\n\n    if (timeLeft &lt; 0) {\n        timerDisplay.textContent = \"Time's up!\";\n        clearInterval(timerInterval);\n    }\n}\n\nconst timerInterval = setInterval(updateTimer, 1000);\n</code></pre>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class='visual-breakdown'>\n    <h2>🎨 Visual Breakdown</h2>\n\n    <h3>Color Palette</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Background: #222 (Dark Gray)</li>\n      <li>Text: #eee (Light Gray)</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>Typography</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Font Family: sans-serif</li>\n      <li>Font Size: 5em (for timer display)</li>\n      <li>Font Weight: Bold (for timer display)</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>Layout</h3>\n    <p>The timer is centered both horizontally and vertically on the page.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class='potential-improvements'>\n    <h2>✨ Potential Improvements</h2>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Add Interactivity:</strong> Include start, pause, and reset buttons to control the timer.</li>\n      <li><strong>Visual Enhancements:</strong> Use a more visually appealing font and add animations or transitions.</li>\n      <li><strong>Customizable Timer:</strong> Allow users to set the initial timer value.</li>\n      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> Implement audio or visual notifications when the timer reaches zero.</li>\n      <li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Ensure the webpage is responsive and looks good on different screen sizes.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class='code-snippets'>\n    <h2>💻 Code Snippets for Improvements</h2>\n    <h3>Adding Start/Pause Buttons (HTML)</h3>\n    <pre><code>&lt;button id=\"startButton\"&g